WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.850
This is one page of a walking pad manual.

2
00:00:03.850 --> 00:00:06.257
Now, watch the same steps.

3
00:00:06.607 --> 00:00:09.792
Run the pad empty, at the lowest speed.

4
00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:12.396
From the rear, compare the two gaps.

5
00:00:12.396 --> 00:00:14.604
Then switch off, and unplug.

6
00:00:15.254 --> 00:00:18.054
There is a bolt in each rear cap.

7
00:00:18.054 --> 00:00:20.795
Each bolt pulls one end of the rear roller.

8
00:00:21.445 --> 00:00:24.940
If the belt is too far right, turn the right bolt clockwise,

9
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.750
a quarter turn.

10
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.090
Too far left? Then use the left bolt.

11
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.115
Take out the tool, and plug in.

12
00:00:34.115 --> 00:00:37.009
Run the belt for two minutes, and look again.

13
00:00:37.009 --> 00:00:39.927
Repeat, until both gaps are the same.

14
00:00:40.577 --> 00:00:43.619
Unplug again. Lift the belt edge in the middle.

15
00:00:43.619 --> 00:00:46.656
It must come up about two to three inches.

16
00:00:48.577 --> 00:00:51.759
If the belt slips, turn both bolts clockwise,

17
00:00:51.759 --> 00:00:53.978
by the same quarter turn.

18
00:00:53.978 --> 00:00:56.948
If it is too tight, turn both back.

19
00:00:57.598 --> 00:01:00.563
Last, put a little silicone oil on the deck,

20
00:01:00.563 --> 00:01:03.505
under the belt, near the center.

21
00:01:03.505 --> 00:01:05.337
Never on top of the belt.

22
00:01:06.148 --> 00:01:08.586
Centered, tight and quiet.

23
00:01:08.586 --> 00:01:10.564
No return, no ticket.
